# Blacklist Hub - HTTP endpoint smoke tests
# Requires the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
#
# The bearer token is read from the local .env file (APP_API_TOKEN) via $dotenv,
# so no secret is stored in this versioned file. If you have no .env, either
# create one (see .env.example) or override @token below with a literal value.
#
# Adjust @host if the app runs elsewhere (the README's Docker example maps 8081:8080).

@host = http://localhost:8080
@token = {{$dotenv APP_API_TOKEN}}

### 1. IPs - authorized (expect 200, text/plain body)
GET {{host}}/blacklist/ips.txt
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2. IPs - missing Authorization header (expect 401, fail-closed)
GET {{host}}/blacklist/ips.txt

### 3. IPs - wrong token (expect 401)
GET {{host}}/blacklist/ips.txt
Authorization: Bearer definitely-wrong-token

### 4. Hashes - authorized (expect 200)
GET {{host}}/blacklist/hashes.txt
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Domains - authorized (expect 200)
GET {{host}}/blacklist/domains.txt
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. URLs - authorized (expect 200)
GET {{host}}/blacklist/urls.txt
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Actuator health - not behind the blocklist token (expect 200)
GET {{host}}/actuator/health
